\[
|S^{=n}| \leq \sum_{i=1}^{k} p_i(n - \lceil \log(k) \rceil)
\]

The right side of the inequality represents a sum of polynomials, which itself is a polynomial, hence confirming that the set \( S \) is sparse.

In conclusion, the construction guarantees sparsity since the combined representation \(\langle x, i \rangle\) intrinsically maintains the sparse nature of each \( S_i \), bounded by a polynomial function based on the total length \( n \) constraint.

